| Comment "
  Rule   : Web Shell Command Execution via PHP-CGI
  Tactic : Execution (TA0002)
  Tech   : T1059.003 - Command and Scripting Interpreter: Windows Command Shell
  Author : Aedan Podest
  Tested : BOTS v1 (index=botsv1)

  Detects cmd.exe spawned by php-cgi.exe — the process chain produced when a
  PHP web shell calls system() or exec() to run OS commands. IIS spawns php-cgi.exe
  to handle PHP requests; php-cgi.exe spawning cmd.exe only happens when PHP code
  explicitly invokes a command shell. This chain has no legitimate use in normal
  IIS/PHP-CGI operation.

  NOTE: In BOTS v1, Sysmon fields are stored as raw XML and are not extracted
  by Splunk. This search uses rex to pull Image, ParentImage, and CommandLine
  from _raw. In a production environment with Sysmon field extraction configured,
  replace the rex commands with direct field references (ParentImage, Image,
  CommandLine) and remove the keyword pre-filter.
"

index=botsv1 sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" earliest=0
    "<EventID>1</EventID>" "php-cgi.exe" "cmd.exe"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='ParentImage'>(?<ParentImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Computer>(?<Computer>[^<]+)</Computer>"
| where like(lower(ParentImage), "%php-cgi.exe")
    AND like(lower(Image), "%cmd.exe")
| table _time, Computer, ParentImage, Image, CommandLine
| sort _time
